{"kind":"event","event_id":7800,"event_uid":"01M2PDHHXY9Y1J1MG651JD1SPB","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":329,"issue_uid":"01M2PDCSQ7MFJ16QN6T4FFT67W","issue_short_id":"t67w","actor":"exam:2@run-170","hlc_physical_ms":1789606283198,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"36d6ee46ce766dd4f2b5f490d7ac1f9621a0b6adc50ae169b0696f494af1fcba","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2PDHHXXQG2C784NJGWJZK0V","author":"exam:2@run-170","body":"exam for task 2 (derived add command): writing tests/test_ultra_run_add_cmd.py in the shape of tests/test_ultra_run_bootstrap_cmd.py.\n\nPlan, leg by leg:\n- (a)-(d) [M1]: table legs call derive_add_cmds(tmp_path) on file-presence trees; exact tuple equality against the pairs and rules M1 names. Plus one leg for M1's 'never runs anything' clause: _pip_externally_managed and subprocess.run both patched to raise on a requirements.txt tree.\n- (e)-(g) [M2]: in-process calls to add_command_stage(args_file, receipt, stage, root) on a real args file written under tmp_path, with a recording stage callable of the driver's own shape (ultra_run.py 537-540) and a plain receipt dict; args file read back off disk, bytes compared byte-for-byte on the write-nothing legs.\n- (h) [M3]: the real ultra_run.py against a throwaway git repo (package.json + bun.lock), plan with no Dependencies line -> exits 0, add-command row directly after bootstrap-command, dirty-baseline directly after it, no addCmd/addDevCmd/addCmdSource anywhere.\n- (i)/(j) [M3]: ultra_run.py copied into a temp dir beside a stub compile_plan.py that execs the real compiler by absolute path with the same argv and then adds the shared dependencies literal to both the emitted args file and the JSON it printed — the HERE seam at line 593, since Task 1's compiler is absent from this clone. (i) green run stamps bun add / bun add -d / detected:bun-lockfile in args.json, stdout receipt and receipt.json; (j) bare package.json refuses: non-zero, no receipt.json, last row add-command ok False naming package-json, no dirty-baseline row.\n\nExpected red at BASE: ImportError on derive_add_cmds/add_command_stage.","created_at":"2026-09-17T00:51:23.197101300Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T00:51:23.198Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7801,"event_uid":"01M2PDJ2REK35KAX08JJCDJK6K","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":328,"issue_uid":"01M2PDCPCY4EGV68CGFNQKC54E","issue_short_id":"c54e","actor":"impl:1@run-170","hlc_physical_ms":1789606300430,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"80b2a8e8d5d81db4ddcf95d85a677eb35243f8c18abacb2107a219ed056be147","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2PDJ2RDJCV5QB1WAKG6HTPX","author":"impl:1@run-170","body":"Task 1 approach: mirror the declared exam command (#644) shape exactly — DEPENDENCIES_LABEL_RE beside EXAM_COMMAND_LABEL_RE, parse_dependencies/dependencies_violations reading through _plan_header_value, joined into grammar_violations at the compile path (stderr, exit 1) and into collect_violations for --check. The --check branch additionally mirrors the dependencies refusals onto stderr, because M4 pins that channel and collect_violations prints its verdict list on stdout. The compiled key rides result and args_payload conditionally — absent, not null, when the header has no line. Then one paragraph in ultrawrite SKILL.md §The document after the Exam command paragraph, and one - **Dependencies:** bullet in greenfield-stack.md §The two knobs. No test file of my own: tests/test_compile_plan_dependencies.py is the peer's exam.","created_at":"2026-09-17T00:51:40.429424989Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T00:51:40.43Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7802,"event_uid":"01M2PDM69PYMY2T3ZHEMT9YC0D","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":328,"issue_uid":"01M2PDCPCY4EGV68CGFNQKC54E","issue_short_id":"c54e","actor":"exam:1@run-170","hlc_physical_ms":1789606369590,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"00da25d47368314a7a2239fcda00d95dc3f73c1b873c3802ead642f7feafc2f6","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2PDM69MQP1QPCDNPK6P8HJD","author":"exam:1@run-170","body":"exam (task 1, tests/test_compile_plan_dependencies.py) — approach.\n\nOne pytest file in the shape of tests/test_compile_plan_edges.py: a real one-task claims-v1 plan written to tmp_path with its gate-verdict record written by extract_gate_input.gate_input, parameterized on the header **Dependencies:** line, compiled by a subprocess and read off stdout / the --emit-args file / the exit code / stderr. Legs (a)-(f) call the two module-level functions directly (sys.path.insert on skills/ultrapowers/scripts, then compile_plan.parse_dependencies / compile_plan.dependencies_violations), so BASE fails them as AttributeError on the absent name rather than as an ImportError on the module.\n\nVerified at BASE: the template plan checks PLAN OK and compiles rc 0 both with and without the header line — so the header line is inert at BASE and every red below is the absent feature, not a malformed fixture. evals/fixtures/claims/plan.md compiles rc 0 with --emit-launch/--emit-args (leg (h) is the one leg green at BASE, being the no-key case).\n\nTwo readings I am pinning, so a later session does not have to reconstruct them:\n\n1. Leg (i)/M4 say --check prints the refusal on STDERR. Every other --check violation in this compiler goes to STDOUT (main() line ~2932 prints collect_violations' strings with a bare print; only the plain-compile grammar path at ~3049 uses file=sys.stderr). The Proof says stderr, so the exam asserts stderr, and the implementer must route the dependencies: strings there under --check as well. I am not substituting stdout for it: that would leave M4 unproven. Flagging it here because it is the one place this task's clause diverges from the house shape.\n\n2. Leg (f) 'yields a string beginning dependencies: naming dev: twice' — read as: the both-dev defect yields exactly one string, beginning dependencies:, that names the dev: marker. The exam asserts len==1, the prefix, and that dev: appears in it; it does not pin a count of the substring inside the message, which would be pinning wording the clause does not give. The both-empty message is asserted as one dependencies: string matching (?i)no package|empty, for the same reason.","created_at":"2026-09-17T00:52:49.588701790Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T00:52:49.59Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7803,"event_uid":"01M2PDNMHAAMDA22KNDYX9Y986","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":329,"issue_uid":"01M2PDCSQ7MFJ16QN6T4FFT67W","issue_short_id":"t67w","actor":"exam:2@run-170","hlc_physical_ms":1789606416938,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"16826ad528e4b04dec26b5e20ca08b4b3533fb463a9438ab5e058d5859eab41d","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2PDNMH9PM1AX3TJ0CCTN4CK","author":"exam:2@run-170","body":"exam written: tests/test_ultra_run_add_cmd.py, 21 tests, every Proof leg (a)-(j) covered, each assertion tagged with its leg and clause.\n\nRed at BASE for exactly one reason: `ImportError: cannot import name 'add_command_stage' from 'ultra_run'` at collection — the produced symbols do not exist yet. Nothing else in the file is unresolved (the plan fixture, the gate-verdict artifact, the stub-compiler seam and the git repo fixtures were all exercised).\n\nValidated outside this tree: against a scratch reference implementation of derive_add_cmds + add_command_stage + the main wiring, all 21 pass, including the three driver legs. Two mutants confirmed caught: (1) stamping when nothing is declared -> leg (f) x2 and leg (h) go red; (2) the stage moved after dirty-baseline -> legs (h), (i), (j) go red.\n\nReadings a later session would otherwise reconstruct:\n- Leg (h) vs the global constraint 'runs byte-for-byte as at BASE for a plan with no Dependencies line': the leg is explicit that the add-command row IS present (ok True, 'no dependencies declared') on such a run, so the constraint is read as being about the args file and the stamped keys, not about the stages list. The exam asserts the row's presence and that none of addCmd/addDevCmd/addCmdSource appears in the args file, the stdout receipt or receipt.json.\n- 'the one recorded row' in legs (e)-(g) is asserted as len(rows) == 1: the stage function records exactly one row per call.\n- Leg (e)'s 'its other keys unchanged' is asserted as set(after) - set(before) == {addCmd, addDevCmd} plus value equality on every pre-existing key; legs (f)/(g)'s 'bytes identical' is a read_bytes() comparison, so a reformatting rewrite is red.\n- M1's 'never runs anything' clause gets its own leg: _pip_externally_managed and subprocess.run are both patched to raise while the requirements.txt rung is derived, since that is the rung where the bootstrap ladder probes PEP 668.\n- The stub compiler finds the args file from its own argv (--emit-args), execs the real compiler by absolute path, and patches both the emitted args file and the JSON it prints. No env var or PATH shim is involved.\n\nNo unsatisfiable legs.","created_at":"2026-09-17T00:53:36.937181486Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T00:53:36.938Z"}
